{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1489414-exalted-talents","id":1489414,"title":"Exalted Talents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-07T08:48:47-07:00","id":1489414,"title":"Exalted Talents","content":"Inspired by a question that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> recently raised (how to treat Talents as a kind of magic user?), I found myself revisiting an idea near and dear to my heart: the concept of the \u201cupgraded Talent\u201d as TC's counterpart to the Exalted. <br /> <br /> Where a psion or psiad can be thought of kind of like a wizard and a Nova can be thought of as a kind of demigod, the \u201cupgraded Talent\u201d can be thought of as a master of his art. He can take the supposedly mundane skills that he has and can achieve miraculous results. <br /> <br /> It turns out that there's a remarkably easy way to model this in-game: in settings that <i>don't</i> feature mesmerists or stalwarts, allow \u201cupgraded Talents\u201d to design \u201cAptitude Masteries\u201d that mimic some Dynamic or Psychic Gifts found in TC: Adventure!. This <i>can</i> be as simple as changing the keyword, but sometimes requires some changes to the prerequisites. Some examples: <br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Ascetic Trance: as a Psychic Gift, this has the Biological and Momentary keywords, and requires two dots of Integrity. As an Aptitude Mastery, replace the Biological keyword with the Aptitude (Integrity) keyword. It's no longer something she can do because she has a psychic ability to control her body; it's something she can do because the self-discipline that her Integrity represents now extends to control over her autonomous bodily functions. <br /> <br /> Cloud the Mind: as a Psychic Gift, this has the Cognitive keyword and requires two dots of Larceny. As an Aptitude Mastery, replace the Cognitive keyword with the Aptitude (Larceny) keyword. It's not a psychic ability to conceal yourself; is just that you're <i>that good</i> at blending in. <br /> <br /> Sleight of Will: as a Psychic Gift, this has the Energetic keyword and requires a dot of Larceny and the Telekinetic Summoning Gift. As an Aptitude Mastery, it replaces the Energetic keyword with Aptitude (Larceny) and removes the Telekinetic Summoning requirement. But in exchange, an additional condition is needed: the object to be conjured must be hidden where it is, and can only be conjured to somewhere where it's hidden. <br /> <br /> Signal and Noise: as a Dynamic Gift, this has the Attribute (Composure) keyword and requires two dots of Composure. As an Aptitude Mastery, replace the Attribute (Composure) keyword with the Aptitude (Enigmas) keyword and change the prerequisites from Composure \u2022\u2022 to Composure \u2022, Enigmas \u2022\u2022. You're <i>really</i> good at spotting obscure connections and patterns in information. Think of the chalkboard scenes in A Beautiful Mind.</div><br /> Masteries should generally lean toward Aptitude (Skill) keywords, although there are a few that might be Aptitude (Attribute) instead. Psychic Gifts which already have Skill prerequisites are the easiest to turn into Masteries; Dynamic Gifts are designed to operate through Attributes, and adapting them as Masteries generally require swapping out a dot or two of the Attribute requirement with twice as many dots in a suitable Skill. There are some \u201cbest fit\u201d defaults for this: Dexterity Gifts generally work with skills like Aim, Athletics, or Larceny; Stamina, Composure, and Resolve can usually translate to Integrity; Intellect Gifts tend to work well with Enigmas, Humanities, or Science; Manipulation Gifts translate nicely to Persuasion; Presence Gifts to Command; Cunning Gifts to Empathy or Enigmas; and so on. But there's are merely suggestions. <br /> <br /> Dynamic Power Gifts and Psychic Energetic Gifts generally don't make sense as Aptitude Masteries; but a few do, such as Blocking Bullets or Inspired Genius. As always, the Storyguide is the final arbiter of what is and isn't allowed. Take the setting into account: when up against Novas, the Storyguide is encouraged to be more permissive than in the \u00c6on era, for example. In general, if the Gift can be viewed as a side effect of the Talent <i>doing things</i> (e.g., blocking attacks or talking to people), it's probably permissible; if the Gift <i>is</i> what the character would be doing (e.g., firing off energy bolts or entering dreams), it probably isn't. <br /> <br /> And don't forget that Talents can be master craftsmen: while they can't create Powered Super Science, they can create both Advanced and Inspired Super Science. If you want a more mystical bent to them, let them turn their Super Science to Artifacts of Enigmatic Power or Mystical Practices (found in Adventure! and \u00c6ther, respectively). <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T16:00:52-07:00","id":1489437,"title":"","content":"...I have no recollection of raising this question, but cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T21:09:39-07:00","id":1489449,"title":"","content":"I raised this issue in Talent Players Guide topic - however, I do not like it, a bit. 'Mesmerists are wizards' just on basic rules. 'Novas are demigods' just on basic rules. For Talents we need to steal powers from other splats, so they become Exalted? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T21:55:40-07:00","id":1489451,"title":"","content":"I didn't come up with it with the idea of stealing. I originally was going to say, \u201chey, why don't we start coming up with new Masteries for Talents that reflect taking their Skills to impossible lengths?\u201d I even started putting together a list of examples of how each Skill might be supercharged. I had things like \u201csupercharged Integrity might allow you to take your self-discipline to the extreme where you can control even the normally automatic bodily functions\u201d, or \u201csupercharged Survival might let you understand animals so well that you can actually converse with them\u201d. I had an example worked up for every skill except Humanities and Technology. <br /> <br /> And then I looked at the Psychic Gifts. Just a brief look, at first, and then more in-depth. And you know what? Every single one of my \u201csupercharged skills\u201d ideas was <i>already implemented</i>, either as a Psychic Gift or as a Dynamic Gift. <br /> <br /> The issue isn't that the notion of supercharged skills is bad; it's that Adventure! assigned everything potentially like that to mesmerists and stalwarts. <br /> <br /> So I figured: why reinvent the wheel? Since we already <i>have</i> the Gifts I was going to suggest for this, why not just use them? <br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> get where you're coming from, though, which is why I suggested doing this only in settings that don't have stalwarts or mesmerists. In those settings, recreating Psychic and Dynamic Gifts as Aptitude Masteries doesn't trample on anyone; it just expands the repertoire of the \u201cExalted\u201d Talent, making Gifts available that would otherwise go unused. <br /> <br /> Again, these are Gifts that are conceptually an excellent fit for the \u201cExalted Talent\u201d concept; and I'm not going to say that the Talent shouldn't be offered those Masteries just because mesmerists and stalwarts got there first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-08-2022, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T01:57:29-07:00","id":1489458,"title":"","content":"Agree in every way with Dataweaver. It is not that the Talents are coping the others or stealing their powers, the same way a Nova is not coping a Psion when using Quantum Anima as Telekinesis, they just happen to have similar powers that can use the same mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T09:30:12-07:00","id":1489487,"title":"","content":"I'll also note that Masteries were introduced in TC: Assassins, where their most significant difference from Gifts is that Masteries <i>can</i> do impossible things, whereas Gifts are limited to the extremely unlikely. Basically, Assassins <i>are</i> an example of the \u201cExalted Talents\u201d concept I'm going for here; it's just that they're hyper-focused on the genre of \u201cprofessional killers\u201d, while I'm generalizing the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T09:58:45-07:00","id":1489488,"title":"","content":"I think Assassins while focused in assassination, have a interesting variety of masteries, specially in the Preparation (also but less in the evaluation) phase, with a lot about collecting information, hiding/disguise and interacting with people. They are not many but they show assassins can do some close to supernatural actions, not directly linked to killing people (used for that, but not actively killing people with it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T10:19:50-07:00","id":1489491,"title":"","content":"Right. Part of generalizing it either involves dropping the phases or reimagining them: reimagining them would involve replacing \u201cthe Hunt\u201d with something more generic, like a Quest. For this thread, I opted to drop them; so Preparation, Evaluation, and Execution(?) go away, and the only durations available are Constant and Momentary, leaving only the question of how to adapt Masteries with the Hunt duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T10:35:31-07:00","id":1489493,"title":"","content":"Quest duration? Why not?<br /> Much of the idea of Talents is related to story telling, and so a quest would fit greatly to the idea. Also guides a more fantastic feeling to the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T10:56:19-07:00","id":1489495,"title":"","content":"Again, I asked that in the context of abandoning the Hunt framework that Assassins uses. If you keep said framework, but broaden it to a more generic \u201cQuests\u201d (or \u201cMissions\u201d, etc.) arrangement, then Hunt duration isn't a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T12:33:56-08:00","id":1529332,"title":"","content":"I apologize for necro-ing this thread, but I would like to see more examples of Gifts. Which gifts can be reasonably altered for example...almost all of the Dynamic Gifts for sure for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T03:20:54-08:00","id":1529693,"title":"","content":"<i>All Creatures Great and Small</i> could be recast as a Mastery counterpart to <i>Rosetta Stone</i> (TC p.201), to represent the likes of Doctor Doolittle. I might even make the latter a prerequisite for the former, instead of or in addition to Survival. <br /> <br /> <i>Three Moves Ahead,</i> <i>Check!</i>, and <i>Counter-Gambit</i> can be adapted to represent Sherlock Holmes' combat style from the recent(?) movies. <br /> <br /> <i>Command the Many Meridians</i> is a natural fit. <br /> <br /> <i>Dead Men Tell Some Tales</i> can be reframed as a \u201cProfiler\u201d thing, likely based off of Medicine. <br /> <br /> <i>Face of Clay</i> could be reworked to represent being impossibly good at disguising yourself. <br /> <br /> There are, of course, more; this was just what I came up with in the fifteen minutes I had this morning between waking up and getting ready for work. I didn't even get through half of the Biological Psychic Gifts. <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> The other thing to note is that the upcoming <b>Trinity Continuum Player's Guide</b> adapts a few of the Masteries from <b>Assassins</b> as Gifts. The lesson here is that not every <b>Assassins</b> Mastery represents doing something impossible; when looking them over for the purpose of \u201cExalted Talents\u201d, that should be kept in mind. That said, I'm going to assume for now that <b>TCPG</b> has ferreted out all of the ones that ought to be Gifts rather than Masteries; so if you don't find it in <b>TCPG</b> (once it comes out), it's probably <i>not</i> a Gift. <br /> <br /> Finally, this thread predated the <b>TC: Aegis</b> Kickstarter, which I think will be another fabulous source to raid for ideas once the book hits publication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T10:41:33-08:00","id":1547110,"title":"","content":"Sorry for bumping this thread, but can anyone come up with more examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","user":"ryu238","date":". 12-17-2024, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-18T13:52:46-08:00","id":1547133,"title":"","content":"If you don\u2019t mind to check my books in my signature, Quantum Inspiration (in the Powered Inspiration bundle) has my version of Novas using Inspiration and Gifts, and in the same bundle Psychic Inspiration presents Psions and Psiads using Inspiration and Gifts. The first is more versatile, while the second is more interactive on itself.<br /> <br /> Also in my Fists of Flux (in the Fists and Tomes bundle) you have many ways to create your own techniques, what looks a lot like the powers of Exalted, particularly celestial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}